        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Sydney</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1788 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">A British settlement was established at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-cove">Sydney Cove</a> on 26 January 1788 by Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip">Arthur Phillip</a> with the First Fleet; the colony of New South Wales was proclaimed on 7 February 1788. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-australians">Aboriginal Australians</a> had lived in the region for at least 30,000 years.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">Around Port Jackson (Sydney Harbour) on the Pacific coast of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, in a coastal basin between the Tasman Sea and the Blue Mountains, in New South Wales.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Gadigal and the other clans of the Eora; the First Fleet of 1788; a penal colony and then the capital of New South Wales; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> of 1789; the resistance of Pemulwuy; the Rum Rebellion; the Harbour Bridge; the Opera House</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Sydney is the capital of the state of New South Wales and the largest city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>.</span></div>
